      "text": "Notice 1: Westridge Community Center Facilities & Class Registration\nThe Westridge Community Center offers a diverse range of evening educational and recreational workshops for local residents. Registration for all courses must be finalized at least 48 hours before the scheduled start date. Tuition fees are 100 percent refundable if cancellation notification is received in writing at least 7 days prior to the first session. Late cancellations received within 7 days receive a 50 percent credit voucher valid for future enrollment within 12 calendar months. Participants must present proof of municipal residency at the main administrative office upon arrival.\n\nNotice 2: Public Library Digital Media & Computer Lab Access Rules\nLibrary cardholders in good standing are entitled to access high-speed workstation computers for up to 2 hours per day. Computer sessions can be extended by 30 minutes if no other patrons are waiting in queue. Printing services cost 15 cents per page for standard black-and-white documents and 50 cents per page for color prints. Downloading executable installer files or attempting to bypass network security filters is strictly prohibited and results in immediate suspension of library privileges. All user files must be saved onto external USB storage drives as local workstation hard drives automatically reset and erase stored data every evening at midnight.\n\nNotice 3: Municipal Recycling and Organic Waste Disposal Regulations\nResidential households must separate solid waste into designated color-coded collection bins. Blue bins are reserved for clean paper, cardboard, glass bottles, and aluminum cans. Green bins accept organic food waste, coffee grounds, and garden trimmings. Plastic bags, film wrap, household batteries, and electronic waste must not be placed in curb collection bins and must instead be dropped off at the central Municipal Transfer Station on Saturdays between 8:00 AM and 4:00 PM.",
